# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings.
#
# This project is developed on Windows, where editors produce CRLF, but it is
# meant to be cloned on macOS and Linux too. Without this file, git commits
# whatever it is handed, and a repository ends up with a mix — which turns a
# one-line change into a diff that claims the whole file was rewritten.
#
# `text=auto` tells git to store every text file with LF in the repository and
# convert to the platform's native ending on checkout. Windows users still get
# CRLF in their working copy; the committed form stays consistent.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

* text=auto

# Explicit for the file types this project actually contains, so the intent is
# readable rather than inferred.
*.ts   text
*.js   text
*.json text
*.css  text
*.html text
*.md   text
*.txt  text
*.svg  text

# Binary: never convert these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
